<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]bank_service_savings_limits

This table outlines the monetary limits for various types of banking services available to different customer segments, specifically highlighting savings for individuals, senior citizens, and differently abled customers. The table consists of four columns, detailing the 'Type of service' alongside the respective savings limits for 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. There are two rows under the main categories of services: 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery'. For both service types, the savings limits are specified as '20,000 per instance' for individuals and senior citizens/differently abled customers, while current account customers have a significantly higher limit of '5 lacs per instance'. The data illustrates a clear distinction in treatment among different customer groups, with current account customers receiving a notable increase in savings limits, potentially indicating a tiered service provision based on account type. The footnote indicates that these values are subject to change based on bank policy, highlighting the dynamic nature of banking services. Overall, the table answers questions regarding the monetary constraints tied to specific banking interactions and the variations applied across different customer categories.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786701052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
